      "short": "to drip",
      "usage": "distil, drop (down).",
      "full": "H7491. raaph [ רָעַף ] verb trickle, drip , synonym of נזל , II. ערף (compare Arabic flow (of blood), bleed (of the nose)); — Qal Imperfect 3masculine plural יִרְעֲפוּ , of clouds Job 36:28 (with עֲלֵי person; || יִזְּלוּ ), with accusative of material טַל Prov 3:20 ; figurative דָּ֑שֶׁן יִרְעֲפוּן מַעְגָּלֶיךָ Psa 65:12 (i.e. fertilizing rain); subject of moistened ground, מִדְבָּר נְאוֺת , 65:13 . Hiph`il Imperative masculine plural הַרְעִיפוּ Isa 45:8 trickle , O heavens, from above (figurative: || צֶרֶק יִּוְּלוּ ).",
